1. Definitions
1.1 Software
“Software” means the proprietary Bonezegei Scripting Language interpreter and runtime distributed by the Developer, including, where applicable:
a.	executable and binary files;
b.	the official installer;
c.	portable distributions;
d.	command-line tools;
e.	runtime components;
f.	standard libraries supplied by the Developer;
g.	documentation and examples;
h.	updates, patches, and upgrades; and
i.	other files expressly identified as part of Bonezegei.
The Software does not include User-created Scripts or Applications.
Third-party components included with the Software may be governed by separate license terms.
1.2 Script
“Script” means source code, instructions, configuration, or other content written in or for the Bonezegei Scripting Language.
1.3 Application
“Application” means any software program, system, service, product, package, or other work created by a User that:
a.	contains or executes one or more Scripts;
b.	uses or invokes the Software;
c.	includes the Software or part of an authorized Software distribution; or
d.	otherwise depends upon the Bonezegei runtime.
1.4 Portable Copy
“Portable Copy” means a copy of the Software that can be used or deployed without running the official Bonezegei installer.
A Portable Copy may include a ZIP archive, portable directory, deployment package, container image, virtual-machine image, or similar package.
1.5 Official Channels
“Official Channels” means the following Developer-controlled contact and distribution channels:
Website:	https://bonezegei.com
